---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/ui/PageHero.astro";
import Pricing from "../components/sections/Pricing.astro";
import siteConfig from "../../site.config";
---

<Base
  title={`Pricing — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description="Lyrica pricing, what is included, the refund position and the current open-beta offer."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Pricing"
    title={siteConfig.pricing.mode === "paid" ? "One price. No subscription." : "Free while it is in beta."}
    lead={
      siteConfig.pricing.mode === "paid"
        ? "A single one-time license, updates included, with a 14-day refund window. No account, no recurring charge."
        : "Every style, Desktop Scene and the Stream window are free during open beta. A Discord account is required to download and gets one free key; the app itself needs no account."
    }
  >
    <a href="/compare" class="btn btn-primary h-10 px-4">Compare options</a>
    <a href="/requirements" class="btn btn-ghost h-10 px-4">Check requirements</a>
  </PageHero>

  <Pricing />

  <section class="pb-20">
    <div class="wrap max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-xl tracking-[-0.03em]">What “free beta” means here</h2>
      <div class="prose-lyrica mt-4 text-sm">
        <p>
          The app is fully usable and does not expire. There is no trial countdown, no feature
          locked behind a payment and no card form. A Discord sign-in gates the installer and issues
          one free license key. That key is checked by the app.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a paid version launches, existing beta keys keep working under the terms published at
          that time. We will not silently turn a free install into a subscription. Any future price,
          gift option and refund window will appear on this page before checkout opens.
        </p>
        <p>
          Gift checkout and the referral programme are closed today because there is nothing to buy.
          The buttons on the pricing card are placeholders until those programs are enabled in
          configuration with a real hosted checkout.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
